&lt;h6 data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;6658&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;#LI-Remote&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/h6&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SeatGeek believes live events are powerful experiences that unite humans. With our technological savvy and fan-first attitude we’re simplifying and modernizing the ticketing industry.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By catering to both consumers and businesses, we’re powering a new, open entertainment ecosystem where fans have effortless access to experiences, and teams, venues, and shows have seamless access to their audiences. Because everyone should expect more from ticketing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make your mark&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring Data Analyst Interns to join us for summer 2027. As a member of the Analytics team, you will develop questions, conduct exploratory analyses, build data models in our data warehouse, and create dashboards in Looker and Mixpanel. Over twelve weeks, you’ll work closely with Business, Product, Design, and UX stakeholders, gaining experience with the fast-paced live events industry. Above all, you will develop a deep understanding of SeatGeek’s business and help ensure that that understanding is at the heart of our forward-looking strategy. &lt;em&gt;This is a 12-week summer Internship Program with a hybrid work style. You will be expected to be on-site 50% of the week at our corporate office in NYC.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop expertise in core Analytics competencies, including exploratory data analysis, insight generation, reporting, KPI definition, and A/B testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage first-class AI dev tools to build out measurement frameworks, develop key reporting, and collaborate with engineers to drive rapid iteration of features, bringing ideas to life faster than ever before&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate key learnings and recommendations to stakeholders in a manner that productively influences decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with senior members of the Data Team to develop and execute business stakeholder roadmaps&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evangelize data expertise, best practices, and documentation within the Data team and in collaboration with our business partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a currently enrolled college student set to graduate in the spring/summer of 2028, ideally studying economics, psychology, computer science, statistics, mathematics, or another quantitative discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid business acumen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaboration skills and familiarity with using data points to build a narrative to guide business strategy and inform decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building reports within a business intelligence tool is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;$360 per quarter to spend on tickets to live events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly commuter card for transportation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subscription to Headspace&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free lunch &amp;amp; snacks is provided every day in the office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Weekly planned events like comedy/broadway shows, sports games, museum visits and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Housing stipend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;**Please note you are expected to come into the SeatGeek New York City Office at least 3 days a week**&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;The compensation for this role is $45/hour USD (based on a 40 hour work week).&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;SeatGeek is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment regardless of race, color, religion, creed, age, national origin or ancestry, ethnicity, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, military or veteran status, or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. As an equal opportunities employer, we recognize that diversity is a positive attribute and we welcome the differences and benefits that a diverse culture brings. Come join us!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;To review our candidate privacy notice,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://seatgeek.com/privacy/USApplicantNotice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://seatgeek.com/privacy/USApplicantNotice&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;click here.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SeatGeek believes live events are powerful experiences that unite humans. With our technological savvy and fan-first attitude we’re simplifying and modernizing the ticketing industry. &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the VP of Engineering, the Director of Engineering will lead the engineering organization responsible for the systems at the core of how teams, venues, and promoters manage tickets and operate their businesses. Hundreds of major live event venues around the globe rely on the SeatGeek platform, including those home to the Dallas Cowboys, Cleveland Cavaliers, Florida Panthers, and Manchester United F.C.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will set technical direction for this complex, mature platform while helping lead its evolution toward SeatGeek’s next generation of products and architecture. At the same time, you will help change how we build software as we move toward an AI-native engineering organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires someone who can move comfortably between technology, product, and the ticketing domain. You will partner closely with Product and Design leadership, Engineering Managers, Senior Engineers, and our clients to turn complicated business problems into clear technical and product direction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set technical direction across US Ticketing, working with Engineering Managers and Staff+ engineers on architecture, system ownership, modernization, and platform boundaries&lt;/li&gt;
