&lt;h6&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;#LI-Remote&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/h6&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SeatGeek believes live events are powerful experiences that unite humans. With our technological savvy and fan-first attitude we’re simplifying and modernizing the ticketing industry. &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is central to making SeatGeek&#39;s Helpdesk and core IT systems proactive by default, powered by automation and AI-driven self-service. You will build smart automations, turn tricky escalations into scalable learnings and solutions, and configure best-in-class AI and automation systems for maximum impact. You’ll take ownership of the employee experience as the technical driver of how employees get help, and how recurring issues are prevented - harnessing demand patterns and data to make support feel seamless.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll help build an excellent technology experience today while creating the systems and operating patterns needed for a thoughtful AI-amplified future. The right person ruthlessly challenges the status-quo, and is equally comfortable designing and building an automated workflow, debugging an access issue, or walking into a conference room before a meeting to make sure everything is humming. You’ll also play a visible role in our NYC office, helping make conference rooms, shared spaces, all-hands meetings, and everyday workplace technology dependable and easy to use.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build for an AI-amplified future by designing, launching and improving helpdesk and automation workflows with an eye towards faster and higher quality issue resolution&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be proactive: own the support and automation operating model and use demand patterns and service data to improve intake, knowledge, self-service, routing, documentation, root-cause resolution, and continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate stakeholder needs and data analysis into practical solutions, rollout plans, documentation, and durable operating processes while partnering with vendors and internal stakeholders to resolve issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver amazing hands-on service by owning complex escalations across hardware, software, access, identity, applications, and endpoints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own employee technology systems and the NYC workplace experience at our flagship office, including device lifecycle, procurement, vendors, licensing, conference rooms, shared spaces, AV, all-hands support, planned events, onboarding, and employee-lifecycle workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in automation engineering, IT/Helpdesk support and operations, system + workflow configuration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intensely dissatisfied with the status quo - manual, repetitive processes genuinely bother you, and you can&#39;t leave them alone. You&#39;re the person who automates their own work, then comes for everyone else&#39;s&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A fast and fearless learner - you move into unfamiliar tools, systems, and problems quickly and come out the other side dangerous&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relentless automation and AI curiosity - you stay on top of what AI can do, you&#39;ve built or experimented with agents and automations yourself. You have opinions about where it&#39;s genuinely useful and how to leverage AI, automation, tools, APIs and data together to drive transformation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A successful track record of independently owning improvements from problem definition through build, testing, rollout, and follow-up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong troubleshooting experience across hardware, software, identity and access, endpoints, applications, and basic networking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting device lifecycle, procurement, vendors, licensing, or workplace technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong judgment around security, privacy, access, automation safety, and when to escalate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in person in the NYC office, including occasional planned event coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nice to have: hands on experience with Serval, Okta, Slack, GSuite, Claude, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity stake&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Discretionary annual bonus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unlimited PTO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Up to 16 weeks of fully-paid family leave&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) matching&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Student loan matching program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health, vision, dental, and life insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Up to $25k towards family building, reproductive health services and Gender-affirming care&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;$500 per year for wellness expenses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subscriptions to Headspace (meditation), Headspace Care (therapy), and One Medical&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;$360 per quarter to spend on tickets to live events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual subscription to Spotify, Apple Music, or Amazon music&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
