&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SeatGeek believes live events are powerful experiences that unite humans. With our technological savvy and fan-first attitude we’re simplifying and modernizing the ticketing industry. &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Social platforms are a critical component of SeatGeek&#39;s marketing strategy, because we need to meet live event fans where they are. As an Analyst on the Paid Social and Programmatic team, you&#39;ll play an integral role in growing a channel that spends eight figures annually across Meta, TikTok, Reddit and Snapchat. You&#39;ll bring the inherent excitement and uniqueness of live events to fans in a way that has a direct impact on SeatGeek&#39;s overall user and revenue growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll use both sides of your brain. You&#39;ll develop growth marketing strategies alongside designers, data scientists and engineers, then prove the value of those strategies through rigorous, hypothesis-led measurement. This is a channel where we run real incrementality studies rather than taking platform-reported numbers at face value, so you&#39;ll be involved in building for, and measuring, success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Day-to-day management of paid social campaigns across Meta, TikTok, Reddit and Snapchat&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage variable budgets to maximize scale while hitting ROAS targets, leaning in when performance beats target and pulling back when it doesn&#39;t&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and optimize per-performer campaigns for artists, teams and tours against a constant onsale calendar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run our dynamic and catalog-driven campaigns, working with product feeds and dynamic creative templates to keep thousands of live events served accurately&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and execute experiments and A/B tests across targeting, creative, copy and landing pages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to incrementality and conversion lift studies with our Analytics team, helping design holdouts, interpret reads, and translate results into how we set budgets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with our Creative team on briefs and creative testing, and close the loop with performance results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Engineering on the internal tooling that automates campaign creation, helping define requirements and spot where automation is falling short&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage directly with our platform partners at Meta, TikTok, Reddit and Snap to push their capabilities toward our priorities rather than theirs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of hands-on experience running performance advertising, with meaningful time on Meta and at least one other major social platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing variable, performance-led budgets at scale, where spend flexes against a ROAS or efficiency target rather than being fixed upfront&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An analytical, data-driven background with a proven ability to pull insight and narrative out of large datasets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project and time management skills, so you can hold many campaigns and requests at once without dropping them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communication. You&#39;re at ease explaining a complex strategy to people who don&#39;t live in the ad platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with a data toolbox: spreadsheets plus a BI or analytics tool such as Looker or Hex&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity about measurement. You&#39;ve asked whether a campaign was actually incremental, not just whether the platform reported a good number&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in live entertainment and sports. Knowing who&#39;s hot right now is a genuine advantage in this job&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Discretionary annual bonus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible work environment, allowing you to work as many days a week in the office as you’d like or 100% remotely&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A WFH stipend to support your home office setup&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unlimited PTO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Up to 16 weeks of fully-paid family leave&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) matching&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Student loan matching program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health, vision, dental, and life insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Up to $25k towards family building, reproductive health services and Gender-affirming care&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;$500 per year for wellness expenses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subscriptions to Headspace (meditation), Headspace Care (therapy), and One Medical&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;$360 per quarter to spend on tickets to live events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual subscription to Spotify, Apple Music, or Amazon music&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The salary range for this role is $63,000 - $92,000 USD. In addition, you may receive a discretionary annual bonus based on individual and company performance. Actual compensation packages are based on a wide array of factors unique to each candidate, including but not limited to skill set, years and depth of experience, certifications, and specific location. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
